notes: |
  Single fix commit + packet + witness, found during mobile
  browser verification of editor overlap (412×900) and sample
  load toast behavior.

  1. **CSS padding-top bump (mobile)** — new token
     --app-top-fixed-h-mobile: 108px captures actual rendered
     geometry (56+36+8+59 = 159 from viewport top; padding-top
     159-56+5 buffer = 108). components.css mobile @media
     rule uses the token. cmHost now starts at y=164, with
     5px gap from controlsRow.bottom=159. First 2 lines
     (// Creep, stack() ) fully visible and tappable.

  2. **Toast debounce (SampleLoader multi-bank)** — settle
     timer (TOAST_SAMPLE_SETTLE_MS=1500) in Toast.tsx
     onProgress handler. 3 'loaded' events (one per bank)
     now produce 1 toast showing the last bank's data.
     'error' status cancels pending timer and pushes
     warn-toast immediately (race-safe). SampleLoader
     emit pattern unchanged (3 events per cycle is by design).

  Side-bug found but NOT fixed (out of scope): mobile @media
  rule for .app-controls-row is BEFORE the non-media rule in
  source order, so on mobile the @media rule (padding 4px)
  loses to the non-media rule (padding 6px) by equal specificity
  tie-breaker. controlsRow renders 59px instead of intended
  52px. Fixing this is a separate CSS-organization change.
  Documented in packet.md epistemics; worked around with
  explicit padding-top value.

